// Expected: typeinfer should reject `str == int`.
//
// Same root cause as 04: different type tags are never equal, so this is a
// constant. `int == float` is the one cross-type pair that IS meaningful
// (numeric promotion makes `1 == 1.0` genuinely true) — see
// tests/typeinfer/pass/04_cross_type_ok.tpr, which guards that it stays legal.

str s = "1";
int n = 1;

if (s == n) {
    print("unreachable");
}
